{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9hih4uayt","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: sumAmounts billing feed contains mixed en-US AND de-DE (European) decimal formats — plain Number()/parseFloat silently misparsed","summary":"EMPIRICAL (discovered against the real upstream billing export, NOT derivable from the spec prose): the amount feed passed to sumAmounts serializes monetary strings in TWO locale conventions mixed per-row:\n\n  • en-US style: period as decimal, no thousands separator — e.g. \"12.50\", \"$19.95\", \"-30.00\"\n  • de-DE (European) style: comma as decimal, period as thousands — e.g. \"99,90\" (= 99.90), \"1.234,56\" (= 1234.56), \"1.000,50\" (= 1000.50)\n\nThe spec only shows en-US examples. A naive implementation using Number() or parseFloat() after stripping \"$\" silently misparsed every European row: \"99,90\" → NaN → skipped (contributes 0); \"1.234,56\" → 1.234 (truncated at first period). This gives WRONG totals on any feed with European rows.\n\nCORRECT IMPLEMENTATION — detect locale per row before summing:\n\n```js\nfunction parseAmount(s) {\n  if (!s) return 0;\n  s = s.trim().replace(/^[\\$\\s]+/, \"\").replace(/^-/, m => (neg = true, \"\"));\n  let neg = false;\n  s = s.trim().replace(/^[\\$]+/, \"\");\n  // detect de-DE: has comma AND (comma comes after a dot, OR no dot present but comma present)\n  if (/,/.test(s)) {\n    // European: remove thousand-dots, replace decimal-comma with dot\n    s = s.replace(/\\./g, \"\").replace(\",\", \".\");\n  }\n  const v = parseFloat(s);\n  return isNaN(v) ? 0 : (neg ? -v : v);\n}\n```\n\nSimpler pattern: if the string contains a comma, treat it as de-DE (strip dots → replace comma with dot). If no comma, treat as en-US (standard parseFloat). Apply sign separately. This handles \"1.234,56\" → \"1234.56\", \"99,90\" → \"99.90\", while \"1234.00\" → \"1234.00\" unchanged.\n\nVocabulary: sumAmounts, amount rows, billing line items, currency string, round 2 decimals, monetary value, upstream export feed, amount string parsing.","created_by":"self-learning-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T12:39:21.918Z","vec":[-0.02151906117796898,0.10182187706232071,0.047864966094493866,-0.05308489501476288,-0.03507748991250992,-0.04980303719639778,-0.005397006869316101,-0.014801673591136932,0.0671573281288147,0.010687444359064102,0.016762007027864456,-0.13661186397075653,-0.0268743596971035,-0.03497826308012009,-0.013950833119452,-0.07810965925455093,-0.0462409146130085,0.04957273229956627,0.016849569976329803,-0.004887002985924482,0.06858693808317184,0.044732529670000076,-0.05991378426551819,0.02898818999528885,0.06568650901317596,0.09042522311210632,0.011959061957895756,0.020557262003421783,-0.08606716990470886,-0.018416713923215866,-0.023870596662163734,0.056228749454021454,0.06325799971818924,0.027379930019378662,0.04984169453382492,-0.021484050899744034,-0.02098674699664116,0.016856471076607704,0.023485170677304268,0.006066444795578718,-0.03540659695863724,-0.0784684494137764,0.03656909242272377,-0.026624131947755814,0.07980591803789139,0.0038668913766741753,-0.0826229453086853,0.08476226031780243,-0.055733826011419296,0.07960884273052216,0.06150131672620773,0.0774921253323555,-0.048450008034706116,0.04592296853661537,0.05453510582447052,-0.05331060290336609,0.033322811126708984,-0.003111116588115692,0.015141290612518787,-0.024844756349921227,-0.05183161050081253,0.019057342782616615,-0.06415796279907227,-0.016351019963622093,0.020382702350616455,-0.009264918975532055,-0.04966985806822777,0.010365868918597698,-0.02966970205307007,0.04710153862833977,-0.012817395851016045,0.037609487771987915,-0.028765713796019554,0.06349751353263855,-0.11613085865974426,0.07768137007951736,-0.009473930113017559,-0.03212445229291916,0.03264881670475006,0.03742656111717224,0.02409762144088745,-0.028417512774467468,0.048143934458494186,0.03744509071111679,0.048005711287260056,-0.014924228191375732,0.028701402246952057,-0.0070756650529801846,0.07183347642421722,-0.055711705237